            <ArticleTitle>Rash, fever, and neck pain in the office: is this a neurologic emergency?</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>878-84; quiz 893-4</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Anticonvulsants, neuroleptics, and antispasticity agents are used with increasing frequency in the pediatric population. Each of the drugs discussed in this article has serious but potentially reversible adverse effects. Pediatric primary care providers must be aware of the potential emergencies associated with the use of these neurologic medications to provide prompt and effective treatment.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
